# Canonical Python test-environment input (Project Spec S0301).
#
# The test environment is compiled from repository-owned metadata only; this
# file adds no requirement of its own so that no dependency range has two
# sources of truth:
#
#   api/pyproject.toml                         API/runtime dependencies
#                                              (fastapi, PyJWT[crypto],
#                                              pandas/scikit-learn/joblib pins)
#   pyproject.toml [scientific-forecasting]    statsmodels for the offline
#                                              scientific reproduction tests
#   pyproject.toml [test]                      direct test-only tools
#                                              (pytest, httpx, PyYAML, psycopg)
#
# Regenerate the exact lock with pip-tools under Python 3.12, from the
# repository root, with exactly this command:
#
#   pip-compile --allow-unsafe --strip-extras \
#     --extra=scientific-forecasting --extra=test \
#     --output-file=requirements-test.lock.txt \
#     api/pyproject.toml pyproject.toml requirements-test.in
#
# (pip-compile 7.x echoes its default "--no-index" in the lock header; there it
# only means that no index URL is written into the lock.)
#
# Install it into a fresh Python 3.12 virtual environment with:
#
#   python -m pip install --require-virtualenv -r requirements-test.lock.txt
#   python -m pip check
#
# Never add credentials, private index URLs or local absolute paths here or in
# the lock (tests/test_test_environment_contract.py enforces this).
